    "created_at": "2017-07-11T19:58:17Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-07-11T19:58:17Z",
    "body": "@domenic For continuity, I'd prefer the other browsers to keep the existing `document.open/write` until they make the streaming API available.\r\n\r\nThat being said, I suspect it might be hard to get the consensus on what streaming DOM parsing would be and `document.open/write` are already there and I just don't see a huge conceptual difference between current per-spec `document.open/write` and extending it to detached docs like most of browsers do. I'm concerned that a straightforward and tangible improvement would be swallowed by a much bigger spec work.\r\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
