    "created_at": "2017-07-11T20:39:42Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-07-11T20:40:59Z",
    "body": "[Screenshots](https://www.browserstack.com/screenshots/f08a8f86598cd69ca761c9c5a2daf64987db23e6) confirming @dvoytenko's claim that all major browsers except Firefox support this based on a [trivial test](https://codepen.io/rbyers/pen/owJxgB).\r\n\r\nFiled a [chromium bug](https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=741071) to track the deviation from the spec here.  I don't see an existing UseCounter quantifying the web compat risk of trying to change this, but with (at least) AMP depending on this behavior any measure is likely to be substantial.\r\n\r\nSince 3 browsers already implement this and there's some not-easily-quantified compat risk to changing it, perhaps we should update the spec / tests to match reality in parallel to whatever people want to do with a parser API?  If we want more web compat data confirming this isn't easy to break we could add a UseCounter to chromium then check the HTTP Archive for (non-AMP) sites hitting it during page load, but that'll take a few months to get results for.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
